{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CIK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-open-immersion-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:14ea5f2e2005fb47313a2194ce1491866114162446cca67cc78739153d212272", "source_text": "An open immersion is <ACCENT_0001>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9e2f2a968051e9d92783e887517df3d53d4a92f200fede6ad70748d03704ae79", "unit_id": "tag:0CIP:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CIK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$j : \\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$j$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$U = \\mathcal{U} \\times_\\mathcal{X} X$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$j$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-trivial-implications}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-open-immersion-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e4513bd9e38e516e90eeeb5491185b3801a13518aa23324923cf70a15caca2de", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:66115d8ef629d1884dd5264b8c68acb83136af285d2deec14477e16ad02dfaad", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an open immersion of\nalgebraic stacks. Since <MATH_0002> is representable, it is DM by\nLemma <REF_0001>. On the other hand,\nif <MATH_0003> is a smooth and surjective morphism\nwhere <MATH_0004> is a scheme, then <MATH_0005>\nis an open subscheme of <MATH_0006>. Hence <MATH_0007> is <ACCENT_0001>tale\n(Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>)\nand we conclude that <MATH_0008> is <ACCENT_0002>tale from the definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d327e0f01aca4f2fae3ab6e31933910e242b3593ec38139a9b77d4249ea715c8", "unit_id": "tag:0CIP:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CIK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0005": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$V$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0009": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0010": "$W$", "MATH_0011": "$T \\to W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0012": "$T$", "MATH_0013": "$T \\to W$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0b025c50a6afc1514272533e486dcfb6455af1584cbde6384c090eef04bebb00", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e179de62bb5fa9ab580dd3798188b4880276a41d66870aa6bb0b179282a2dc5c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is <ACCENT_0001>tale,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is DM and for any morphism <MATH_0004>\nwhere <MATH_0005> is an algebraic space and any <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism\n<MATH_0006> where <MATH_0007> is an algebraic space,\nthe morphism <MATH_0008> is <ACCENT_0003>tale,\n<STRUCT_0004> there exists some surjective, locally of finite presentation, and flat\nmorphism <MATH_0009> where <MATH_0010> is an algebraic space and some\nsurjective <ACCENT_0004>tale morphism <MATH_0011>\nwhere <MATH_0012> is an algebraic space such that the morphism <MATH_0013> is <ACCENT_0005>tale.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2c1501927a2bacd6927513914376a34bd1519a9d056ffbf042a95e960d0df5f5", "unit_id": "tag:0CIQ:statement"}
